Why the constructor preserves the scientific subject
==================================================

Fix a prepared role p and its already issued budget B, request Q, gate G and
scientific manifest S. The constructor reads these exact whole byte editions.
It checks Q.Root_import=p.Root_import, Q.budget=G.budget=p.budget and G.request=Q.
It also checks the full worker ROLE, mode, source indices, cohort batch and
original parent-array byte spans. The original preparation review must name
all four emitted import/request/gate/prepared descriptors in its output set.
These are equality and provenance assertions; they do not evaluate parents.

Let c be the literal child argv assembled from S,Q,G,p.out,p.guard. Core's
existing metadata validator checks the prospective launch against c and B's
typed command projection. The new launch L points to B,Q,G and c, while none
of B,Q,G points back to L. Thus the graph of hashes is acyclic and no old
document needs replacement. The literal outer argv consists of the unchanged
profile, B,L, limits and c. If a later genuine guard executes that argv, the
scientific common reader independently joins these same editions and marker.
This constructor makes no assertion that such execution has occurred.

The inherited writer-union calculation adds the caller's raw API records and
bounded encoding images to the ten child rows, leaving shared SDK rows unique.
There are eighty distinct paths and 57,540,737 declared content/allocation bytes,
inside the same256MiB serial invocation reserve. Pairwise disjoint role unions
prevent two selected roles from claiming a single fresh writer slot. Fresh
checks occur again in the actual caller/profile; no output is silently reused.

The qualified preparation-review branch carries its authorship and scope into
the construction receipt and parent IO document. Root's explicit ownership
acknowledges that provenance check; it does not turn it into a second
independent mathematical proof. All model, original membership, numerical
Source/control and future strict/registration obligations remain as before.

These arguments reuse the existing acyclic launch and bounded writer ledger.
They are not a new group-theoretic result, case disposition, conjecture proof,
whole manuscript recovery or measured compression claim.
